        "variant": "guest-progression-feast-pass",
        "html": "<div class=\"progression-page\" data-progression-page=\"feast-pass\" data-companion-context=\"feast-pass\" data-companion-copy=\"Your Feast Pass shows local website activity saved in this browser only.\">\n  <nav class=\"detail-breadcrumb\" aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\"><a href=\"/\">Home</a><span aria-hidden=\"true\">/</span><span>Feast Pass</span></nav>\n  <header class=\"progression-hero\"><p class=\"section-kicker\">TOADAL FEAST &middot; GUEST JOURNEY</p><p class=\"progression-eyebrow\">BROWSER-LOCAL PREVIEW</p><h1>Your Feast Pass</h1><p class=\"progression-lede\">A compact record of your website journey: real page visits, Home Treat finds, configured quests, and completed browser preview scores.</p><p class=\"progression-truth-note\">Progress stays in this browser. There is no connected identity, account sync, server ranking, transferable currency, mobile entitlement, or permanent reward promise. Starter XP and Sparks are editable configuration.</p></header>\n  <section class=\"progression-section\" aria-labelledby=\"pass-status-title\"><div class=\"progression-section-heading\"><div><p class=\"section-kicker\">YOUR LOCAL STATUS</p><h2 id=\"pass-status-title\">Progress snapshot</h2></div><span class=\"progression-local-badge\">Guest &middot; this browser</span></div><dl class=\"progression-stat-grid\"><div class=\"progression-stat\"><dt>Level</dt><dd data-progression-stat=\"level\" aria-live=\"polite\">&mdash;</dd></div><div class=\"progression-stat\"><dt>Total XP</dt><dd data-progression-stat=\"xp\" aria-live=\"polite\">&mdash;</dd></div><div class=\"progression-stat\"><dt>XP to next level</dt><dd data-progression-stat=\"xp-to-next\" aria-live=\"polite\">&mdash;</dd></div><div class=\"progression-stat\"><dt>Sparks</dt><dd data-progression-stat=\"sparks\" aria-live=\"polite\">&mdash;</dd></div><div class=\"progression-stat\"><dt>Home Treats</dt><dd data-progression-stat=\"treats\" aria-live=\"polite\">&mdash;</dd></div><div class=\"progression-stat\"><dt>Daily streak</dt><dd data-progression-stat=\"streak\" aria-live=\"polite\">&mdash;</dd></div><div class=\"progression-stat\"><dt>Page discoveries</dt><dd data-progression-stat=\"discoveries\" aria-live=\"polite\">&mdash;</dd></div><div class=\"progression-stat\"><dt>Quests complete</dt><dd data-progression-stat=\"quests-complete\" aria-live=\"polite\">&mdash;</dd></div></dl><p class=\"progression-storage\" data-progression-storage-status role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">Guest progress is stored only in this browser.</p></section>\n  <section class=\"progression-section progression-daily\" aria-labelledby=\"daily-reward-title\"><div><p class=\"section-kicker\">UTC DAY</p><h2 id=\"daily-reward-title\">Daily check-in</h2><p data-daily-reward-status role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">Check-in availability comes from editable starter configuration.</p></div><button class=\"button-link button-link--primary\" type=\"button\" data-claim-daily disabled aria-disabled=\"true\">Check-in status loading</button></section>\n  <section class=\"progression-section\" aria-labelledby=\"pass-treats-title\"><div class=\"progression-section-heading\"><div><p class=\"section-kicker\">HOME COLLECTION</p><h2 id=\"pass-treats-title\">Feast Treats</h2></div><span class=\"progression-muted\">Three local Home finds</span></div><p>Each unique Home candy maps to one descriptive browser-local Treat. The Golden Block candy is counted only after the block is broken and the revealed candy is collected.</p><div class=\"progression-empty\" data-progression-treat-list data-progression-empty=\"No Treat definitions are configured.\"><p>Treat finds are local collection notes, not paid currency or mobile-game items.</p></div></section>\n  <section class=\"progression-section\" aria-labelledby=\"pass-quests-title\"><div class=\"progression-section-heading\"><div><p class=\"section-kicker\">NEXT STEPS</p><h2 id=\"pass-quests-title\">Configured quests</h2></div><a class=\"text-link\" href=\"/feast-pass/quests/\">Open quest board <span aria-hidden=\"true\">&rarr;</span></a></div><div class=\"progression-empty\" data-progression-quest-list=\"all\" data-progression-empty=\"No quests are configured yet.\"><p>Only recorded route visits, Treat collections, and website-player completions count.</p></div></section>\n  <section class=\"progression-section\" aria-labelledby=\"pass-rewards-title\"><div class=\"progression-section-heading\"><div><p class=\"section-kicker\">LOCAL RECOGNITION</p><h2 id=\"pass-rewards-title\">Milestones</h2></div><a class=\"text-link\" href=\"/feast-pass/rewards/\">View rewards &amp; collection <span aria-hidden=\"true\">&rarr;</span></a></div><div class=\"progression-empty\" data-progression-reward-list><p>Earned and locked states are derived from configured level milestones and real local activity.</p></div></section>\n  <section class=\"progression-section\" aria-labelledby=\"pass-discoveries-title\"><div class=\"progression-section-heading\"><div><p class=\"section-kicker\">PAGE VISITS</p><h2 id=\"pass-discoveries-title\">Discoveries</h2></div></div><div class=\"progression-empty\" data-progression-discovery-list><p>World and Stories visits may appear as local activity; they do not publish lore or mark story completion.</p></div></section>\n  <nav class=\"progression-nav\" aria-label=\"Player pages\"><a href=\"/feast-pass/\" aria-current=\"page\">Feast Pass <span class=\"sr-only\">(current page)</span></a><a href=\"/feast-pass/quests/\">Quests</a><a href=\"/feast-pass/rewards/\">Rewards</a><a href=\"/leaderboards/\">Leaderboards</a><a href=\"/profile/\">Guest profile</a></nav>\n  <section class=\"progression-controls\" aria-labelledby=\"local-controls-title\"><div><h2 id=\"local-controls-title\">Local data controls</h2><p>Clear website progression only. Unrelated cartridge, game, and mobile data are not changed. Account sync is a future state; see <a href=\"/account/\">Account</a>.</p></div><button class=\"button-link button-link--secondary\" type=\"button\" data-clear-progression>Clear website progression</button></section>\n</div>"
